---
import DocsPage from '../../components/DocsPage.astro'
import { sitePath } from '../../data/site-path'
---

<DocsPage
  title="Getting started"
  eyebrow="INTEGRATION GUIDE"
  summary="Create one backend, mount one provider, and let the grid request only the projection it needs."
  alternateLocaleHref={sitePath('zh/docs/getting-started/')}
>
  <h2>1. Choose a backend</h2>
  <p>
    The bundled Worker + Rust/WASM backend is a useful default. A host-owned backend works too when it implements the
    <a href={sitePath('docs/backend-port/')}>backend port</a>.
  </p>
  <h2>2. Mount the provider once</h2>
  <pre><code>{`<SpreadsheetUiProvider backend={backend}>
  <SpreadsheetGrid sheetId={sheetId} viewport={viewport} />
</SpreadsheetUiProvider>`}</code></pre>
  <h2>3. Add capabilities deliberately</h2>
  <p>
    Keep authoritative workbook facts in the backend. Feature-local UI state belongs to atoms; consult the
    <a href={sitePath('docs/atoms/viewport/')}>viewport</a> and
    <a href={sitePath('docs/atoms/selection/')}>selection</a> ownership guides before adding state.
  </p>
</DocsPage>
